            bitfld.long 0x00 12. "SLV_ISO_SAR_DATA_CLK_STRETCH,This bit indicates the Bus hold (clock stretching) in Slave mode with Multiple SAR feature - for isolating the write transfer related data corresponding to one slave address with another slave address" "0: Slave is not holding the bus to isolate..,1: Slave holds the bus to isolate current RX.."
            newline
            bitfld.long 0x00 11. "SDA_STUCK_NOT_RECOVERED,This bit indicates that SDA stuck at low is not recovered after the recovery mechanism" "0: SDA Stuck at low is recovered after recovery..,1: SDA Stuck at low is not recovered after.."
            newline
            bitfld.long 0x00 10. "SLV_HOLD_RX_FIFO_FULL,This bit indicates the BUS Hold in Slave mode due to Rx FIFO is Full and an additional byte has been received (This kind of Bus hold is applicable if IC_RX_FULL_HLD_BUS_EN is set to 1 and bit 9 of the IC_CON register.." "0: Slave is not holding the bus or Bus hold is..,1: Slave holds the bus due to Rx FIFO is full"
            newline
            bitfld.long 0x00 9. "SLV_HOLD_TX_FIFO_EMPTY,This bit indicates the BUS Hold in Slave mode for the Read request when the Tx FIFO is empty" "0: Slave is not holding the bus or Bus hold is..,1: Slave holds the bus due to Tx FIFO is empty"
            newline
            bitfld.long 0x00 8. "MST_HOLD_RX_FIFO_FULL,This bit indicates the BUS Hold in Master mode due to Rx FIFO is Full and additional byte has been received (This kind of Bus hold is applicable if IC_RX_FULL_HLD_BUS_EN is set to 1 and bit 9 of the IC_CON register.." "0: Master is not holding the bus or Bus hold is..,1: Master holds the bus due to Rx FIFO is full"
            newline
            bitfld.long 0x00 7. "MST_HOLD_TX_FIFO_EMPTY,If the IC_EMPTYFIFO_HOLD_MASTER_EN parameter is set to 1 the DW_apb_i2c master stalls the write transfer when Tx FIFO is empty and the the last byte does not have the Stop bit set" "0: Master is not holding the bus or Bus hold is..,1: Master holds the bus due to Tx FIFO is empty"
            newline
